  "separate_science_proposal": {
    "target": "def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface",
    "source_raw_sha256_as_read": "0e67b76725bbe6a1f5ab260eb0e8f43121aae25828a002e3168d7cf6e84e3ce2",
    "actual_finding": "A particular arbitrary counterterm need not cancel when the relative cohomology class vanishes; vanishing supplies some primitive. For a fixed b4, cancellation requires [a4]_F=s[b4]_F. The repaired supplier proves exactly existential sufficiency (steps4.1\u20135.1) and necessity for a cancelling counterterm (step6.1).",
    "exact_old": "Under these hypotheses, that proposition states that $s a_4$ is $d_H$-exact and that shifting $X$ by $-\\hbar^n[b_4]_{\\mathscr F_n}$, for $b_4\\in\\mathcal K_n^{0,4}$, cancels the order-$n$ breaking exactly when $[a_4]_{s|d_H}=0$.",
    "exact_proposed": "Under these hypotheses, that proposition states that $s a_4$ is $d_H$-exact and that there exists an admissible $b_4\\in\\mathcal K_n^{0,4}$ such that shifting $X$ by $-\\hbar^n[b_4]_{\\mathscr F_n}$ cancels the order-$n$ breaking if and only if $[a_4]_{s|d_H}=0$.",
    "scope_preserved": "All conditional K_n, formal Ward nilpotence, compact-support and local-counterterm assumptions retained. General Lie-algebra representation traces still imply no physical anomaly cancellation.",
    "consumer_reading": "Complete ex-qftx-vectorlike-charge-cancellation read: it uses only d and ell trace definitions, not this counterterm existence assertion. Actual full consumer cone must be rebound if root authorizes public Definition repair.",
